{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102784-the-limits-of-fetish-vehicles","id":1102784,"title":"The Limits of Fetish Vehicles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-12T06:03:30-07:00","id":1102784,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The Limits of Fetish Vehicles?","content":"So often instead of entire vehicles becoming a Fetish, the books take an approach where its easier to just make a fetish mast or something. But can you make a Fetish say Boat? You can after all make a Fetish van, though they don't talk about them much. I know with a rank 6/ N/A Fetish you could make a vehicle that does about anything. But could you say make a rank 4-5 Fetish boat for travel? Binding a spirit to something this big is interesting. Could you say have a Fetish power for a vessel be something akin to a mini den realm, possibly interacting with the spirit bound to it. So say a pirate ship where you have a secret mirror layer by walking through the mirror in the captains room, allowing you to hide treasure and crew in this mirror room.<br /> <br /> What about Fetish cars and saddles? What is a good rank say for a Fetish saddle that manifests a spirit/emanation horse in the Umbra? Or that allows a horse that wears it to step sideways with their Rider and travel Airts?<br /> <br /> There was a Wagnerian camp and they seemed to have plans to possible evacuate Gaia to survive the Apocalypse, what type of vehicle would they use to transport kin and packs?<br /> <br /> I feel they ignore the potential Werewolves can have if they horde things on the Penumbral side. Technically for instance they can keep gattling guns or tanks taken from the Battlefield realm, and they remain as long as you don't try to take them to the material world. You could have a decent structure set up then in the Penumbral side with no one the wiser on the material side. Garou making Ships, or Caravans in the Penumbra out of materials from the material world, would such things just become Ephemera from being stored in the Umbra?<br /> <br /> <br /> Ideas? Like I plan to someday to a slight futuristic age game, think Outlaw Star and Cowboy Bebop, and space ships are eventually going to be made into fetishes. But using Glasswalkers methods it would likely be a ship, with different fetish parts, like weapons, and computer systems yeah. So what do you think Garou sailors, like say Bonegnawer pirates, and Fenrir Vikings, what kind of Fetishes would the best captains be creating/discovering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T16:14:48-07:00","id":1102939,"title":"","content":"In the Ratkin book, there is a Level 5 Fetish, the Mystery Machine. It's basically a fetish van whose spirit has been awakened. This lets the ratkin travel around taking their home with them. <br /> <br /> The van runs on gasoline, but can also be powered by Gnosis, letting it run for one day without fuel for each point of Gnosis spent. The driver can also activate the Gift Silent Running 3 times per day, for free, which helps make it impossible to track the van. Finally, flashing the high-beams allows the driver to take the vehicle and everyone inside into the Umbra. There's on a tiny few of those magical vans in the world. <br /> <br /> In theory other tribes of breeds might be able to make something similar.<br /> <br /> So I would say what you're asking is possible, though incredibly rare, to the point that having a full on fetish ship or a bus or a tank or something would be pretty legendary amount the Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T18:19:10-07:00","id":1102972,"title":"","content":"I would also point out that the Ratkin book was kind of silly at times (Freakachu comes to mind), so a Fetish van may or may not actually be feasible in the current edition.<br /> <br /> I agree though that such a thing should be rare/legendary if it were possible at all.<br /> <br /> That van really did have too many abilities for a level 5 fetish imo.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T18:33:51-07:00","id":1102974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102784-the-limits-of-fetish-vehicles?p=1102972#post1102972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also point out that the Ratkin book was kind of silly at times (Freakachu comes to mind)</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. I remember when I was running a Ratkin game and the players wanted to go to the TV zone so they could have a training montage with Goku, Vegeta and the rest of the DBZ characters. Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T18:45:30-07:00","id":1102978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102784-the-limits-of-fetish-vehicles?p=1102974#post1102974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sure. I remember when I was running a Ratkin game and the players wanted to go to the TV zone so they could have a training montage with Goku, Vegeta and the rest of the DBZ characters. Fun times.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was/is a blast for what it was/is.<br /> <br /> My point was that just because a Fetish van appears in that book, doesn't necessarily mean that such things can be done in a game that isn't going for that kind of tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T19:14:01-07:00","id":1102986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102784-the-limits-of-fetish-vehicles?p=1102978#post1102978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that just because a Fetish van appears in that book, doesn't necessarily mean that such things can be done in a game that isn't going for that kind of tone.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. I guess if the ST feels it's in theme for their game to have fetish vehicles, there's that one to act as precedent, but you're absolutely right that it wouldn't be appropriate for all games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T21:54:03-07:00","id":1103012,"title":"","content":"The problem with most modern vehicles is that they are probably too delicate to survive the process. Now, pre-1980s automobiles, sailing vessels, and even 1930s airships could probably work as fetishist vehicles. I would not be surprised if a few Glass Walkers 'liberated' a Zeppelin or three before they were destroyed by the victors in WWI and squirreled them away in the Umbra. Imagine the surprise of a Pentex executive when an airship does a bombing run on his office by dipping out of the Umbra for a few moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T11:36:57-07:00","id":1105780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1102784-the-limits-of-fetish-vehicles?p=1103012#post1103012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with most modern vehicles is that they are probably too delicate to survive the process. Now, pre-1980s automobiles, sailing vessels, and even 1930s airships could probably work as fetishist vehicles. I would not be surprised if a few Glass Walkers 'liberated' a Zeppelin or three before they were destroyed by the victors in WWI and squirreled them away in the Umbra. Imagine the surprise of a Pentex executive when an airship does a bombing run on his office by dipping out of the Umbra for a few moments.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T07:46:14-07:00","id":1107631,"title":"","content":"Never really allowed a player to turn an entire vehicle into a fetish out of the vehicle granted by Genreal Lee totem from Revised Tribebook: Bone Gnawer. Normally it single pieces of the car. Tires that the lower the difficulty of running on awkward surfaces or grant gifts like Silent Running. Gas tanks that can funnel the drivers Gnosis or Rage into it to make the car run longer. Engines that do the silent running thing mentioned above. Fogs Lights that that allow you to see through the veil while they are on. Steering wheels the lower the difficulty of Drive rolls when doing crazy stunts.<br /> <br /> I was working on a North American tribe idea focused around Motorcycle gangs and had a whole list of ideas for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}